{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_COMM_SECTION_7_2_ComM_channel_state_machine","src":"manifest","doc":"SWS_COMManager","page":61,"text":"7.2 ComM channel state machine\n[SWS_ComM_00979]\nUpstream requirements: SRS_ModeMgm_09243\n⌈If the optional PNC functionality is enabled (see [ECUC_ComM_00839]), all PNC\nactions shall be performed before the channel related actions are executed.⌋\n[SWS_ComM_00980]\nUpstream requirements: SRS_ModeMgm_09243\n⌈If the parameter ComMPncNmRequest is set to TRUE (see [ECUC_ComM_00886]), if\nthe \"FULL Communication\" is requested due to a change in the PNC state machine to\nCOMM_PNC_REQUESTED (see [SWS_ComM_01068]) API Nm_NetworkRequest() shall\nbe called, even if the current state is already \"Full communication\".⌋\nRationale: It is the trigger to enable the NM to transmit the NM message immedi-\nately n-times (n=configurable) to ensure a wake up and a synchronization of the PNC\ntransceiver.\n[SWS_ComM_00051]\nUpstream requirements: SRS_ModeMgm_09080\n⌈ComM shall implement one channel state machine for every communication channel\nindependently.⌋\nNote to [SWS_ComM_00051]: The channel state maching is shown in Figure 7.7 and\nan overview of the requirements for the channel state machine transtions is listed in\nTable 7.1\nRationale for [SWS_ComM_00051]: Needed communication capability of channels\nmay be different, thus the controlling must be independent.\nUse Case for [SWS_ComM_00051]: On an ECU with CAN and LIN channel, only the\nLIN requires full communication to request e.g. sensor values while the CAN remains\ninactive.\nCOMM_FULL_COMMUNICATION\nCOMM_NO_COMMUNICATION\nCOMM_SILENT_COMMUNICATION\nCOMM_FULL_COM_READY_SLEEP\nCOMM_FULL_COM_NETWORK_REQUESTED\nCOMM_NO_COM_NO_PENDING_REQUEST\nCOMM_NO_COM_REQUEST_PENDING\n\u0001\n\u0002\n\u0003\n\u0004\n\u0006\n\u0007\n\b\n\u0007\n\u0003\n\b\n\u000e\n\u0002\n\u000f\n\u0001\n\b\n\u0010\n\u0011\n\u0001\n\u0011\n\u0012\n\u0001\n\b\n\u0010\n\u0013\n\u0014\n\u0015\u0016\n\u0006\n\u000f\n\u0017\n\u0012\n\u0018\n\u0016\n\u0006\n\u000f\n\u0002\n\u000e\n\u0019\n\u0016\n\u000f\n\u001a\n\u0007\n\u0002\n\u0001\n\u0011\n\u001b\n\u0001\n\u0012\n\u001b\n\u0001\n\u0013\n\u001a\nComM_RequestComMode(<user>,\nCOMM_FULL_COMMUNICATION)\n[Communication limitation\ndisabled]\nComM_RequestComMode(<user>,\nCOMM_FULL_COMMUNICATION)\n[EcuM entered RUN for the channel]\n[CommunicationAllowed=TRUE]\nComM_<Bus>SM_BusSleepMode(ChX)\n[ComMNmVariant = SLAVE_ACTIVE or\nSLAVE_PASSIVE]\nComM_…","caption":"7.2 ComM channel state machine","sha":null,"series":[{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_COMM_SECTION_7_2_ComM_channel_state_machine","releases":["R23-11"],"page":58,"hash":"0dfd7c99d032b8be","caption":"","screenshot_path":"_src/spec/snippets/assets/a87a3ee9f5c0/page_58.webp"},{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_COMM_SECTION_7_2_ComM_channel_state_machine","releases":["R24-11"],"page":67,"hash":"914c66f1c4369c41","caption":"","screenshot_path":"_src/spec/snippets/assets/564560db2899/page_67.webp"},{"id":"SNIP_CLASSIC_COMM_SECTION_7_2_ComM_channel_state_machine","releases":["R25-11"],"page":65,"hash":"a1481471413353fc","caption":"","screenshot_path":"_src/spec/snippets/assets/26b7e44e6d3d/page_65.webp"}],"releases":["R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"screenshot_path":"_src/spec/snippets/assets/26b7e44e6d3d/page_65.webp","trel":"R25-11","tstat":"section","kind":"snippet","platform":"classic","targets":[{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_ComM_00051] im Text von SWS_COMManager.","rel":["R25-11"],"id":"SWS_ComM_00051"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_ComM_00069] im Text von SWS_COMManager.","rel":["R25-11"],"id":"SWS_ComM_00069"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_ComM_00071] im Text von SWS_COMManager.","rel":["R25-11"],"id":"SWS_ComM_00071"},{"role":"constitutive","conf":0.95,"rt":"EXPLICIT_REFERENCE","m":"","why":"Direktzitat [SWS_ComM_00073] im Text von SWS_COMMa